# Never commit — this repository is PUBLIC.
#
# facts.yaml is the private fact base: defensibility grades, `[RETIRED — false
# claim]` tombstones, clarify_notes, the "MUST be able to defend" lists and the
# AI-assisted flags. Publishing it under Harsh's name would be worse than the
# problem the revamp fixed. The build reads it locally at prebuild; it is not
# bundled and does not need to be tracked here.
#
# Both files were already untracked, so this loses nothing — it just stops
# `git add -A` from staging them. If either ever needs versioning, do it in a
# private repo, or `git add -f` deliberately.
facts.yaml
portfolio-revamp-v2-plan.md
